// Issue #2229 (4th M-2d collision site): the entry file. `shared` here and
// `shared` in `other.brink` are two DIFFERENT knots that happen to share a
// bare name — legitimate M-2d coexistence (`native_module_path` derives a
// distinct module per file, so `insert_symbol` lets them coexist, #790),
// not a duplicate-definition error. Both declare an unlabeled choice at the
// identical structural position inside the knot body, which is exactly the
// shape `stamp_container_ids`'s per-knot loop used to hash WITHOUT a
// per-file qualifier (unlike `root_content_scope_path`'s `#file:{path}`
// prefix for root-level containers, #1504) — producing the identical
// synthetic `DefinitionId` for both files' choices and tripping the #1673
// duplicate-id `E060` codegen guard the moment the whole project's
// container trees were walked.
//
// `main`'s own playthrough never enters `shared` (this fixture's whole
// point is a project-wide COMPILE-time collision, not a runtime one — see
// `stamp_container_ids`, which walks every knot in every file
// unconditionally regardless of reachability), so the golden transcript
// below stays choice-free, satisfying this corpus's own straight-line-only
// contract (`tier1_native.rs`'s module doc / `drive_native_transcript`).

flow main() {
  Hello from the entry.
  -> END
}

flow shared() {
  {?
    * unlabeled choice -> shared_end
  }
}

flow shared_end() {
  Unreached.
  -> END
}
